ationid": "106379401", "author": {"steamid": "76561198101708469", "personaname": "Nobunaga", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198101708469/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 18, "playtime_forever": 1094, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 1039, "last_played": 1645324279, "avatar": "093152cef1092d2149c1b0592c586f40cc558fbb"}, "language": "english", "review": "If you want coop zombie shooting save your money and just buy Left 4 Dead 1 & 2 (they are $2 right now). If you already have Left 4 Dead, just play that, it's more fun than this.\n\nPros:\n-graphics\n-more types of melee weapons than in left 4 dead (I think?)\n\nCons:\n-somehow, they actually managed to make the bots WORSE than they were in Left 4 Dead. It will actively sabotage you. Startle crows, alert the horde, block you, etc. \n-no LAN play no offline play, game over if your wifi goes out or if you take a break\n-menus too complicated, it takes a few minutes and lots of clicking just to set up a private game with friends\n-no custom maps, which was one of the best parts of left 4 dead\n-most weapons are bad until you accumulate upgrades, so grabbing a new weapon when you run out of ammo is not really a thing\n-card system adds complexity without being fun, plus the cards are mostly useless aesthetic cards you are forced to buy in order to unlock good ones\n-the characters are very bland\n-no real creativity or new ideas in terms of level design - scavenge this item, go to this location, etc.\n-recycled maps", "timestamp_created": 1640292406, "timestamp_updated": 1640293906, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 7, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.54278874397277832", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1634050800", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "106379164", "author": {"steamid": "